   1:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** /**
   2:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @file    stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c
   4:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @brief   RCC HAL module driver.
   6:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *          This file provides firmware functions to manage the following
   7:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *          functionalities of the Reset and Clock Control (RCC) peripheral:
   8:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *           + Initialization and de-initialization functions
   9:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *           + Peripheral Control functions
  10:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *
  11:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   @verbatim
  12:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  13:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****                       ##### RCC specific features #####
  14:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  15:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  16:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       After reset the device is running from Internal High Speed oscillator
  17:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (HSI 16MHz) with Flash 0 wait state, Flash prefetch buffer, D-Cache
  18:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       and I-Cache are disabled, and all peripherals are off except internal
  19:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       SRAM, Flash and JTAG.
  20:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) There is no prescaler on High speed (AHB) and Low speed (APB) busses;
  21:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           all peripherals mapped on these busses are running at HSI speed.
  22:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) The clock for all peripherals is switched off, except the SRAM and FLASH.
  23:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) All GPIOs are in input floating state, except the JTAG pins which
  24:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           are assigned to be used for debug purpose.
  25:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  26:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  27:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       Once the device started from reset, the user application has to:
  28:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the clock source to be used to drive the System clock
  29:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (if the application needs higher frequency/performance)
  30:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the System clock frequency and Flash settings
  31:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the AHB and APB busses prescalers
  32:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Enable the clock for the peripheral(s) to be used
  33:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the clock source(s) for peripherals which clocks are not
  34:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           derived from the System clock (I2S, RTC, ADC, USB OTG FS/SDIO/RNG)
  35:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  36:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****                       ##### RCC Limitations #####
  37:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  38:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  39:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       A delay between an RCC peripheral clock enable and the effective peripheral
  40:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       enabling should be taken into account in order to manage the peripheral read/write
  41:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       from/to registers.
  42:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) This delay depends on the peripheral mapping.
  43:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) If peripheral is mapped on AHB: the delay is 2 AHB clock cycle
  44:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           after the clock enable bit is set on the hardware register
  45:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) If peripheral is mapped on APB: the delay is 2 APB clock cycle
  46:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           after the clock enable bit is set on the hardware register
  47:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  48:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  49:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       Implemented Workaround:
  50:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) For AHB & APB peripherals, a dummy read to the peripheral register has been
  51:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           inserted in each __HAL_RCC_PPP_CLK_ENABLE() macro.
  52:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  53:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   @endverbatim
  54:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ******************************************************************************
