 116:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** /** @defgroup RCC_Exported_Functions_Group1 Initialization and de-initialization functions
 117:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *  @brief    Initialization and Configuration functions
 118:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *
 119:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   @verbatim
 120:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ===============================================================================
 121:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** ##### Initialization and de-initialization functions #####
 122:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ===============================================================================
 123:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
 124:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       This section provides functions allowing to configure the internal/external oscillators
 125:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (HSE, HSI, LSE, LSI, PLL, CSS and MCO) and the System buses clocks (SYSCLK, AHB, APB1
 126:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       and APB2).
 127:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 128:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] Internal/external clock and PLL configuration
 129:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) HSI (high-speed internal), 16 MHz factory-trimmed RC used directly or through
 130:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           the PLL as System clock source.
 131:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 132:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) LSI (low-speed internal), 32 KHz low consumption RC used as IWDG and/or RTC
 133:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           clock source.
 134:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 135:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) HSE (high-speed external), 4 to 26 MHz crystal oscillator used directly or
 136:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           through the PLL as System clock source. Can be used also as RTC clock source.
 137:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 138:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) LSE (low-speed external), 32 KHz oscillator used as RTC clock source.
 139:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 140:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) PLL (clocked by HSI or HSE), featuring two different output clocks:
 141:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The first output is used to generate the high speed system clock (up to 216 MHz)
 142:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The second output is used to generate the clock for the USB OTG FS (48 MHz),
 143:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****              the random analog generator (<=48 MHz) and the SDIO (<= 48 MHz).
 144:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 145:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) CSS (Clock security system), once enable using the function HAL_RCC_EnableCSS()
 146:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           and if a HSE clock failure occurs(HSE used directly or through PLL as System
 147:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           clock source), the System clock is automatically switched to HSI and an interrupt
 148:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           is generated if enabled. The interrupt is linked to the Cortex-M7 NMI
 149:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (Non-Maskable Interrupt) exception vector.
 150:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 151:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) MCO1 (microcontroller clock output), used to output HSI, LSE, HSE or PLL
 152:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           clock (through a configurable prescaler) on PA8 pin.
 153:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 154:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) MCO2 (microcontroller clock output), used to output HSE, PLL, SYSCLK or PLLI2S
 155:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           clock (through a configurable prescaler) on PC9 pin.
 156:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 157:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] System, AHB and APB busses clocks configuration
 158:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) Several clock sources can be used to drive the System clock (SYSCLK): HSI,
 159:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           HSE and PLL.
 160:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           The AHB clock (HCLK) is derived from System clock through configurable
 161:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           prescaler and used to clock the CPU, memory and peripherals mapped
 162:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           on AHB bus (DMA, GPIO...). APB1 (PCLK1) and APB2 (PCLK2) clocks are derived
 163:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           from AHB clock through configurable prescalers and used to clock
 164:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           the peripherals mapped on these busses. You can use
 165:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           "HAL_RCC_GetSysClockFreq()" function to retrieve the frequencies of these clocks.
 166:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 167:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****       -@- All the peripheral clocks are derived from the System clock (SYSCLK) except:
 168:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (+@) I2S: the I2S clock can be derived either from a specific PLL (PLLI2S) or
 169:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****               from an external clock mapped on the I2S_CKIN pin.
 170:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****               You have to use __HAL_RCC_PLLI2S_CONFIG() macro to configure this clock.
 171:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (+@)  SAI: the SAI clock can be derived either from a specific PLL (PLLI2S) or (PLLSAI) o
 172:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****               from an external clock mapped on the I2S_CKIN pin.
 173:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****                You have to use __HAL_RCC_PLLI2S_CONFIG() macro to configure this clock.
 174:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (+@) RTC: the RTC clock can be derived either from the LSI, LSE or HSE clock
 175:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****               divided by 2 to 31. You have to use __HAL_RCC_RTC_CONFIG() and __HAL_RCC_RTC_ENABLE()
 176:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****               macros to configure this clock.
 177:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (+@) USB OTG FS, SDIO and RTC: USB OTG FS require a frequency equal to 48 MHz
 178:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****               to work correctly, while the SDIO require a frequency equal or lower than
 179:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****               to 48. This clock is derived of the main PLL through PLLQ divider.
 180:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (+@) IWDG clock which is always the LSI clock.
 181:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** @endverbatim
 182:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @{
 183:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   */
 184:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 185:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** /**
 186:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @brief  Resets the RCC clock configuration to the default reset state.
 187:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @note   The default reset state of the clock configuration is given below:
 188:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *            - HSI ON and used as system clock source
 189:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *            - HSE, PLL, PLLI2S and PLLSAI OFF
 190:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *            - AHB, APB1 and APB2 prescaler set to 1.
 191:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *            - CSS, MCO1 and MCO2 OFF
 192:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *            - All interrupts disabled
 193:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @note   This function doesn't modify the configuration of the
 194:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *            - Peripheral clocks
 195:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *            - LSI, LSE and RTC clocks
 196:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @retval None
 197:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c ****   */
 198:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_rcc.c **** HAL_StatusTypeDef HAL_RCC_DeInit(void)
